{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794791544,"nonce":"hgWP1ZxwTOMCPh47q+/8NfBjqFg=","title":"An idle window renders about 60 frames per second on Wayland (keep-alive), each 1.1 to 1.7 ms in the render phase","message":"Live probe (nested KWin, fs-tasks and fs-calendar release builds): with nothing happening, F0/F1 frame markers arrive every 16.7 ms and each frame costs 1.1 to 1.7 ms (p4 render), rebuild=false, no animation. That is the intended keep-alive of event_loop/lifecycle.rs (comment there: about 7 percent CPU, avoids the 1 s swapchain starvation), but the work per idle frame is a full render phase, not a present of the cached layer.\nEffect: continuous GPU and CPU use of an idle desktop app, and the frame the user's key lands in is queued behind one of these.\nProposal (to discuss with the maintainer first): when nothing changed, re-present the last texture without running phase 4, or present at a lower rate once idle.","files":null}]}